      { "text": "A baseline complete blood count to document hemoglobin and reticulocyte trend.", "explanation": "Incorrect. While a baseline CBC may be reasonable supportive care, the lecturer's specifically required pre-prescription test is G6PD testing. This would be the correct answer if asking the test used to follow chronic hemolysis after primaquine initiation in a known deficient patient." },
      { "text": "Hepatic function panel including transaminases and direct bilirubin levels.", "explanation": "Incorrect. Hepatic monitoring is more relevant for atovaquone-proguanil (which can elevate transaminases) and is not the lecturer's mandated test before 8-aminoquinoline therapy. This would be the correct answer if asking which baseline test is most relevant before starting Malarone." },
      { "text": "Serum pregnancy testing to exclude early gestation prior to dosing.", "explanation": "Incorrect. Although primaquine and tafenoquine are contraindicated in pregnancy because of the risk of fetal hemolysis if the fetus has G6PD deficiency, this would not be relevant for a male patient. Pregnancy testing would be the correct answer only if the patient were a female of reproductive age." }
